@*
    Question Sets (org-assurance-question-sets).

    NOTE 2026-11-15: this file was rebuilt from the compiled Web build of
    2026-11-15 18:48 (obj/Release/net8.0/PubTmp/Out) after the working copy
    was reset by mistake. Every line of markup, style and script is the
    compiled original; Razor comments are not kept in a build, so
    the in-page comments are gone and this header was rewritten (the part
    from "TWO VIEWS, ONE PARTIAL" on is the original text).

    ENDPOINTS (via the Web proxy /practice/api/org-assurance/*)
        question-sets, question-sets/{id}, question-sets/{id}/questions
        question-sets/{id}/versions, /impact, /new-version, /submit,
        /return, /approve (551)
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/admin-question-types
        GET    /practice/api/org-assurance/evidence-types   (Evidence: Not Applicable or a type)

    TWO VIEWS, ONE PARTIAL
      list -- the organization's question sets (row click / Open / New
              Question Set go to the set page).
      set  -- one set, opened READ-ONLY (view): its details and its
              questions. Actions > Edit switches the same page to edit
              mode (2026-11-05): the details at the top, the questions in an
              editable grid below (2026-11-13: spreadsheet look, no Order /
              Status / Ver columns -- rows keep their entry order). "Add Row"
              inserts a blank row; each
              row's Guidance / Expected Evidence open under it. ONE Save
              writes the details, then the whole grid (520's
              sp_org_assurance_question_set_questions_save: update, add,
              and remove the rows taken out). New / edited rows are marked
              until saved. Save / Cancel return to the view.
              Owner is not asked; Delete is not offered on this screen.
              (Question Status: see 561 below.)
      561 (2026-11-15, sir -- Audit Change spec 4.2.3): the row's
      "Description / Guidance" is now TESTING GUIDANCE -- the field for test
      procedures, simple or step-by-step (help_text, longer box) -- and the
      grid has a Status column again (Active / Inactive; a new row starts
      Active). An Inactive question stays in the set but is not taken into
      an execution; the list's Questions / Mandatory / Total Weight count
      Active questions only. The read-only view shows Status too.
      ?new=1 opens a new set directly (the Audit Definition page's "Add new
      question set" link, 2026-11-05). This partial is no longer hosted on
      the Audit Definition page.

    The 516 Question Repository (and its Category / Subcategory) was
    withdrawn by 520: questions belong to their set again.

    551 (2026-11-14, sir) -- VERSIONS AND APPROVAL
      A question set is a master: it is approved, and changed only by a new
      version. Each version is its own set row (same code, its own
      questions). Version status: Draft -> Under Review (Recommend) ->
      Active (Approve); Return sends it back to Draft; approving makes the
      previous Active version Superseded. Only a Draft is edited.
        List      one row per set -- its latest version: Version, Status.
        Menus     View; Edit / Recommend / Discard Draft (Draft);
                  Approve / Return (Under Review); New Version (Active).
        Set page  Version facts; "Audits using this question set" for a
                  Draft / Under Review version -- what approving it will do
                  to each audit (moved in its draft, or a new audit version
                  for review); the set's Versions (click one to view it).
      Backend (551): GET question-sets/{id}/versions, /impact;
      POST question-sets/{id}/new-version, /submit, /return, /approve;
      DELETE question-sets/{id} discards a Draft v2+.

    558 (2026-11-14): the .qs-grid spreadsheet rules are shared with My
    Audits and live in practice-management.css; the #qsSetView rules below
    are this page's own.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1>@Model.Title</h1>
        <p>@Model.Description</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel" id="qsUnavailable" hidden>
    <div class="pm-empty">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-clipboard-list pm-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2 id="qsUnavailableTitle">Question Sets are not available for this organization.</h2>
        <p id="qsUnavailableBody">Ask a GRAC Admin to enable <code>screen.org-assurance-question-sets</code>.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pm-panel" id="qsRoot" hidden>

    <div id="qsListView">
        <div class="pm-toolbar" style="flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
            <select id="qsFilterOrganization"><option value="">Loading organizations...</option></select>
            <input id="qsSearch" type="text" placeholder="Search set name / code..." />
            <button class="pm-button icon" id="qsRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
            <button class="pm-button primary" id="qsAddSetBtn" type="button">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> New Question Set
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="qsListMessage" style="display:none;"></div>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap" style="margin-top:12px;">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Code</th>
                        <th>Name</th>
                        <th>Version</th>
                        <th style="text-align:right;">Questions</th>
                        <th style="text-align:right;">Mandatory</th>
                        <th style="text-align:right;">Total Weight</th>
                        <th>Status</th>
                        <th></th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="qsSetBody">
                    <tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load sets.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-pager" data-pager="qs-set">
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="prev" type="button">Previous</button>
            <span data-pg="label">Page 1</span>
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="next" type="button">Next</button>
            <span data-pg="total" class="pm-pager-total">0 total</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="qsSetView" hidden>
        <div class="pm-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="qsBackBtn">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Back to Question Sets
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="qsActionsBtn" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" hidden>
                <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt" aria-hidden="true"></i> Actions
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:10px; margin-left:2px;"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="qsSetMessage" style="display:none;"></div>

        <div id="qsSetRead">
            <h3 class="qs-section">Question Set Details</h3>
            <dl class="qs-facts" id="qsReadFacts"></dl>
            <h3 class="qs-section">Questions <span class="pm-badge" id="qsReadCount">0</span></h3>
            <div class="pm-table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="width:120px;">Code</th>
                            <th>Question</th>
                            <th>Response Type</th>
                            <th style="text-align:center;">Mandatory</th>
                            <th>Evidence</th>
                            <th style="text-align:right;">Weight</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody id="qsReadBody"></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div id="qsImpact" hidden>
                <h3 class="qs-section">Audits using this question set <span class="pm-badge" id="qsImpactCount">0</span></h3>
                <div class="pm-message qs-impact-note" id="qsImpactNote"></div>
                <div class="pm-table-wrap">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>Audit</th><th>Version</th><th>Status</th><th>Uses set version</th><th>When this version is approved</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody id="qsImpactBody"></tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="qs-section">Versions</h3>
            <div class="pm-table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th style="width:80px;">Version</th><th>Status</th><th style="text-align:right;">Questions</th><th>Change Note</th><th>Recommended</th><th>Approved</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody id="qsVersionBody"></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="qsSetEdit" hidden>
        <h3 class="qs-section">Question Set Details</h3>
        <div class="qs-details">
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Code <span class="required">*</span></span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="qsSetCode" type="text" maxlength="80" />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field">
                <span>Name <span class="required">*</span></span>
                <input class="pm-input" id="qsSetName" type="text" maxlength="240" />
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field" id="qsSetStatusField" hidden>
                <span>Status</span>
                <select class="pm-input" id="qsSetStatus">
                    <option value="Active" selected>Active</option>
                    <option value="Draft">Draft</option>
                    <option value="Inactive">Inactive</option>
                </select>
            </label>
            <label class="pm-field qs-wide">
                <span>Description</span>
                <textarea class="pm-input" id="qsSetDescription" rows="2" maxlength="4000"></textarea>
            </label>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-grid-head">
            <h3 class="qs-section">Questions <span class="pm-badge" id="qsQuestionCount">0</span></h3>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="qsAddRowBtn">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add Row
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap">
            <table class="qs-grid">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width:130px;">Code <span class="required">*</span></th>
                        <th>Question <span class="required">*</span></th>
                        <th style="width:170px;">Response Type <span class="required">*</span></th>
                        <th style="width:96px;">Mandatory</th>
                        <th style="width:160px;">Evidence</th>
                        <th style="width:84px;">Weight</th>
                        <th style="width:110px;">Status</th>
                        <th style="width:84px;"></th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="qsGridBody"></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="pm-dialog-actions qs-footer">
            <span class="pm-hint" id="qsDirtyNote" hidden>Unsaved changes</span>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="qsCancelBtn">Cancel</button>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="qsSaveBtn">Save</button>
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    #qsSetView .qs-section {
        margin: 16px 0 8px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--fg-secondary);
    }
    #qsSetView .qs-details {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; align-items: start;
    }
    #qsSetView .qs-details .qs-wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
    /* 2026-11-13: spreadsheet look -- the cells carry the lines, the inputs
       have no border of their own; the focused cell is outlined. The general
       .qs-grid rules are in practice-management.css since 558 (shared with
       My Audits' Answer Questions); the rules below are this page's own. */
    #qsSetView .qs-grid textarea.pm-input { resize: none; min-height: 48px; line-height: 1.4; overflow: hidden; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid tbody td.qs-row-tools { padding: 6px; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid tr.qs-new  > td:first-child { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--success-500, #22c55e); }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid tr.qs-edit > td:first-child { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--warning-500, #f59e0b); }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid tr.qs-more td { background: var(--neutral-50); padding: 8px 10px; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid tr.qs-more .pm-input { border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--bg-surface); }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid .qs-more-fields { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; }
    /* 561: Testing Guidance and Expected Evidence -- the same height (4 rows); long text scrolls inside the box. */
    #qsSetView .qs-grid .qs-more-fields { align-items: start; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid .qs-more-fields textarea.pm-input { overflow-y: auto; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid .qs-row-tools { white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid .qs-row-tools .pm-button { padding: 2px 8px; }
    #qsSetView .qs-grid .qs-ver { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-muted); padding-top: 8px; display: inline-block; }
    #qsSetView .qs-footer { align-items: center; }
    #qsSetView .qs-facts {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 260px));
        gap: 8px 20px; margin: 0 0 4px; padding: 12px 14px;
        background: var(--neutral-50); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    }
    #qsSetView .qs-facts .qs-wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    #qsSetView .qs-facts dt { font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    #qsSetView .qs-facts dd { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--neutral-700); overflow-wrap: anywhere; white-space: pre-wrap; }
    #qsSetView .qs-facts dd.qs-empty { color: var(--fg-subtle); font-style: italic; }
    #qsSetView .qs-read-sub { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-top: 4px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
    /* 551: the impact note reads as a warning; the open version is marked. */
    #qsSetView .qs-impact-note { display: block; background: var(--warning-100, #fef3c7); color: var(--warning-700, #b45309); margin: 0 0 8px; }
</style>

<script src="~/js/Shared/page-actions-menu.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';
    const wf = window.__wfCommon;
    if (!wf) { console.error('__wfCommon missing'); return; }

    const API      = '/practice/api/org-assurance';
    const FEATURE  = 'screen.org-assurance-question-sets';
    const U        = p => String(window.appBasePath || window.pmPathBase || '').replace(/\/+$/, '') + p;
    const pick     = (o, a, b) => o ? (o[a] != null ? o[a] : o[b]) : null;

    const state = {
        orgId          : '',
        search         : '',
        page           : 1,
        pageSize       : 25,
        total          : 0,
        setsById       : {},
        questionTypes  : [],
        evidenceTypes  : [],       // 2026-11-05: Evidence = one of these, or Not Applicable
        // set page
        setId          : null,     // null = new set
        mode           : 'view',   // 'view' | 'edit'
        set            : null,     // the loaded set (owner is kept as it was -- not asked)
        rows           : [],       // grid model: {key, questionId, code, text, help, typeId, mandatory, evidenceTypeId, expected, weight, status, version, open, state:'saved'|'new'|'edit'}
        dirty          : false
    };
    let rowKey = 0;
    let openMenuEl = null, openMenuTrigger = null;

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot);
    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') boot();

    async function boot() {
        wf.wirePager('qs-set', function (delta) {
            const next    = state.page + delta;
            const maxPage = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(state.total / state.pageSize));
            if (next < 1 || next > maxPage) return;
            state.page = next; reloadSets();
        });

        const orgs = await wf.loadOrgs();
        if (!orgs.length) {
            wf.unavailable('qsUnavailable', 'qsUnavailableTitle', 'qsUnavailableBody',
                'No accessible organizations', 'Contact your GRAC Admin.');
            return;
        }
        wf.populateOrgSelect('qsFilterOrganization', orgs);
        state.orgId = document.getElementById('qsFilterOrganization').value || '';

        const enabled = await wf.checkFeature(FEATURE, state.orgId);
        if (!enabled) {
            wf.unavailable('qsUnavailable', 'qsUnavailableTitle', 'qsUnavailableBody',
                'Question Sets are not available for this organization.',
                'Ask a GRAC Admin to enable ' + FEATURE + '.');
            return;
        }
        document.getElementById('qsRoot').hidden = false;

        await Promise.all([loadQuestionTypes(), loadEvidenceTypes()]);
        wireControls();
        reloadSets();

        // ?new=1 -- the Audit Definition page's "Add new question set" link
        // (2026-11-05): open straight on a new set.
        try {
            if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('new') === '1') openSet(null, true, 'edit');
        } catch (_) { /* no URL API: stay on the list */ }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Wiring
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function wireControls() {
        document.getElementById('qsFilterOrganization').addEventListener('change', async function (e) {
            if (!(await leaveSetPage())) { e.target.value = state.orgId; return; }
            state.orgId = e.target.value || '';
            state.page  = 1;
            if (!document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden) showList(); else reloadSets();
        });
        document.getElementById('qsSearch').addEventListener('input', function (e) {
            state.search = e.target.value || '';
            state.page = 1;
            clearTimeout(window.__qsSearchTimer);
            window.__qsSearchTimer = setTimeout(reloadSets, 250);
        });
        document.getElementById('qsRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', reloadSets);
        document.getElementById('qsAddSetBtn').addEventListener('click', function () { openSet(null, false, 'edit'); });

        // List: row click opens the set; 3-dot menu as before.
        const body = document.getElementById('qsSetBody');
        body.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            const trg = e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger');
            if (trg && body.contains(trg)) {
                e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
                if (openMenuTrigger === trg) { closeRowMenu(); return; }
                openRowMenu(trg, setMenuItems(trg.getAttribute('data-id')));
                return;
            }
            if (e.target.closest('a, button, input, label, select')) return;
            const tr = e.target.closest('tr.pm-row-clickable[data-id]');
            if (tr && body.contains(tr)) openSet(tr.getAttribute('data-id'), false, 'view');
        });
        document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            if (!openMenuEl) return;
            if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-menu') || e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger')) return;
            closeRowMenu();
        });
        document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) { if (e.key === 'Escape') closeRowMenu(); });
        window.addEventListener('resize', closeRowMenu);
        window.addEventListener('scroll', closeRowMenu, true);

        // Set page
        document.getElementById('qsBackBtn').addEventListener('click', async function () {
            if (await leaveSetPage()) showList();   // from view or edit
        });
        document.getElementById('qsCancelBtn').addEventListener('click', async function () {
            if (state.dirty && !await window.gracUi.confirm('Discard the unsaved changes?',
                  { type: 'warning', title: 'Discard changes', confirmText: 'Discard' })) return;
            // A saved set goes back to its view; a new one back to the list.
            if (state.setId) openSet(state.setId, true, 'view'); else showList();
        });
        document.getElementById('qsSaveBtn').addEventListener('click', save);
        document.getElementById('qsAddRowBtn').addEventListener('click', addRow);
        ['qsSetCode', 'qsSetName', 'qsSetStatus', 'qsSetDescription'].forEach(function (id) {
            document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input', markDirty);
            document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('change', markDirty);
        });

        // 551: a version row opens that version.
        document.getElementById('qsVersionBody').addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            const tr = e.target.closest('tr[data-version-id]');
            if (tr && String(tr.getAttribute('data-version-id')) !== String(state.setId))
                openSet(tr.getAttribute('data-version-id'), false, 'view');
        });

        const grid = document.getElementById('qsGridBody');
        grid.addEventListener('input', onGridEdit);
        grid.addEventListener('change', onGridEdit);
        grid.addEventListener('click', onGridClick);

        if (window.gracPageActions) {
            window.gracPageActions.attach('qsActionsBtn', function () {
                return (state.setId && state.mode === 'view') ? setMenuItems(state.setId)
                    .filter(function (it) { return it.key !== 'view'; })
                    .map(function (it) { return { icon: it.icon, label: it.label, run: it.action }; }) : [];
            });
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Lookups
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function loadQuestionTypes() {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/admin-question-types'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const b = r.ok ? await r.json() : null;
            state.questionTypes = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        } catch (_) { state.questionTypes = []; }
    }
    function typeOptions(selectedId) {
        return '<option value="">' + (state.questionTypes.length ? '-- select --' : '(none published by Admin)') + '</option>'
            + state.questionTypes.map(function (t) {
                const id = pick(t, 'id', 'Id');
                return '<option value="' + wf.escape(id) + '"' + (String(id) === String(selectedId) ? ' selected' : '') + '>'
                     + wf.escape(pick(t, 'name', 'Name') || '') + '</option>';
            }).join('');
    }
    // Evidence (2026-11-05): one input -- "Not Applicable" (no evidence),
    // or the Evidence Type required. Same list as Evidence Config.
    async function loadEvidenceTypes() {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/evidence-types'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const b = r.ok ? await r.json() : null;
            state.evidenceTypes = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        } catch (_) { state.evidenceTypes = []; }
    }
    function evidenceOptions(selectedId) {
        return '<option value="">Not Applicable</option>'
            + state.evidenceTypes.map(function (t) {
                const id = pick(t, 'id', 'Id');
                return '<option value="' + wf.escape(id) + '"' + (String(id) === String(selectedId) ? ' selected' : '') + '>'
                     + wf.escape(pick(t, 'name', 'Name') || '') + '</option>';
            }).join('');
    }
    function evidenceName(r) {
        if (!r.evidenceTypeId) return 'Not Applicable';
        const t = state.evidenceTypes.find(function (x) { return String(pick(x, 'id', 'Id')) === String(r.evidenceTypeId); });
        return t ? (pick(t, 'name', 'Name') || '') : (r.evidenceTypeName || '');
    }

    function typeById(id) {
        return state.questionTypes.find(function (t) { return String(pick(t, 'id', 'Id')) === String(id); }) || null;
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // List
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function reloadSets() {
        const body = document.getElementById('qsSetBody');
        if (!state.orgId) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load sets.</td></tr>';
            wf.updatePager('qs-set', { pageNumber: 1, totalCount: 0, pageSize: 1 });
            return;
        }
        body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        try {
            const qs = new URLSearchParams();
            qs.set('organizationId', state.orgId);
            if (state.search) qs.set('search', state.search);
            qs.set('page', String(state.page));
            qs.set('pageSize', String(state.pageSize));
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/question-sets?' + qs.toString()), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
            const payload = await r.json();
            state.total = Number(payload.totalCount || payload.TotalCount || 0);
            const rows  = payload.rows || payload.Rows || [];
            state.setsById = {};
            body.innerHTML = rows.length ? rows.map(function (row) {
                const id = pick(row, 'questionSetId', 'QuestionSetId');
                state.setsById[String(id)] = row;
                return '<tr class="pm-row-clickable" data-id="' + id + '">'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(pick(row, 'setCode', 'SetCode')) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.escape(pick(row, 'setName', 'SetName')) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + versionCell(row) + '</td>'
                     + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + wf.escape(String(pick(row, 'questionCount', 'QuestionCount') || 0)) + '</td>'
                     // 535: mandatory questions and total weight ('-' before 535 is run).
                     + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + wf.escape(listNumber(pick(row, 'mandatoryCount', 'MandatoryCount'))) + '</td>'
                     + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + wf.escape(listNumber(pick(row, 'totalWeight', 'TotalWeight'))) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + wf.badge(statusLabel(pick(row, 'versionStatus', 'VersionStatus') || pick(row, 'status', 'Status') || 'Active')) + '</td>'
                     + '<td><button type="button" class="pm-action-trigger" data-id="' + id + '" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" title="Actions">'
                     + '<i class="fas fa-ellipsis-v fa-solid fa-ellipsis-vertical" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></button></td>'
                     + '</tr>';
            }).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">No question sets yet. Click "New Question Set" to create one.</td></tr>';
            wf.updatePager('qs-set', { pageNumber: state.page, totalCount: state.total, pageSize: state.pageSize, rowCount: rows.length });
        } catch (err) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Failed to load: ' + wf.escape(err.message || err) + '</td></tr>';
        }
    }

    // 535: a list count / weight -- whole numbers without ".00" (weights are
    // DECIMAL(10,2)); '-' when the value is not there (database before 535).
    function listNumber(v) {
        if (v === null || v === undefined || v === '') return '-';
        const n = Number(v);
        return isFinite(n) ? String(Math.round(n * 100) / 100) : String(v);
    }

    // Row menu items (2026-11-05): View, Edit. The set page's Actions
    // offers the same list minus View. Delete is not offered here.
    // 551: by version status -- Edit / Recommend / Discard Draft for a
    // Draft, Approve / Return for one Under Review, New Version for an
    // Active one (when no version is in progress).
    function versionInfo(id) {
        const s = String(id) === String(state.setId) && state.set ? state.set : (state.setsById[String(id)] || {});
        return {
            status : pick(s, 'versionStatus', 'VersionStatus') || 'Active',
            number : Number(pick(s, 'versionNumber', 'VersionNumber') || 1),
            open   : pick(s, 'openQuestionSetId', 'OpenQuestionSetId')
        };
    }
    function setMenuItems(id) {
        const v = versionInfo(id);
        const items = [
            { key: 'view', icon: 'fa-eye', label: 'View', action: function () { openSet(id, false, 'view'); } }
        ];
        if (v.status === 'Draft') {
            items.push({ key: 'edit', icon: 'fa-pen', label: 'Edit', action: function () { openSet(id, String(id) === String(state.setId), 'edit'); } });
            items.push({ key: 'submit', icon: 'fa-paper-plane', label: 'Recommend', action: function () { recommend(id); } });
            if (v.number > 1) items.push({ key: 'discard', icon: 'fa-trash', label: 'Discard Draft', action: function () { discardDraft(id); } });
        }
        if (v.status === 'UnderReview') {
            items.push({ key: 'approve', icon: 'fa-check', label: 'Approve', action: function () { approve(id); } });
            items.push({ key: 'return', icon: 'fa-rotate-left', label: 'Return to Draft', action: function () { returnToDraft(id); } });
        }
        if (v.status === 'Active' && !v.open)
            items.push({ key: 'newversion', icon: 'fa-code-branch', label: 'New Version', action: function () { newVersion(id); } });
        return items;
    }

    function statusLabel(s) { return s === 'UnderReview' ? 'Under Review' : (s || ''); }
    // List: "v2", plus the Active version when the latest is still in progress.
    function versionCell(row) {
        const n = pick(row, 'versionNumber', 'VersionNumber');
        if (!n) return '';
        const vs = pick(row, 'versionStatus', 'VersionStatus');
        const act = pick(row, 'activeVersionNumber', 'ActiveVersionNumber');
        return 'v' + wf.escape(n) + ((vs === 'Draft' || vs === 'UnderReview') && act
            ? ' <span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">(v' + wf.escape(act) + ' Active)</span>' : '');
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 551: version actions
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function loadImpact(id) {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/question-sets/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '/impact?organizationId='
                + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId)), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const b = r.ok ? await r.json() : null;
            return (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        } catch (_) { return []; }
    }
    function impactLines(rows) {
        return rows.map(function (d) {
            return '- ' + (pick(d, 'definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode') || '') + ' ' + (pick(d, 'definitionName', 'DefinitionName') || '')
                 + ': ' + (pick(d, 'actionText', 'ActionText') || '');
        }).join('\n');
    }
    async function setAction(id, action, body) {
        return postJson('/question-sets/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '/' + action,
            Object.assign({ organizationId: Number(state.orgId), note: null, actor: null }, body || {}));
    }
    async function afterAction(id, mode, text) {
        if (!document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden) {
            await openSet(id, true, mode || 'view');
            wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', text, 'ok');
        } else {
            reloadSets();
            wf.setMessage('qsListMessage', text, 'ok');
        }
    }
    function actionFailed(err) {
        const msg = err.message || String(err);
        if (!document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden) wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', msg, 'error');
        else wf.setMessage('qsListMessage', msg, 'error');
    }

    async function newVersion(id) {
        if (!await window.gracUi.confirm('Create a new Draft version of this question set? It starts as a copy of the Active version; the Active version stays in use until the new one is approved.',
              { type: 'confirm', title: 'New version', confirmText: 'Create' })) return;
        try {
            const j = await setAction(id, 'new-version');
            const nid = j.questionSetId || j.QuestionSetId;
            await openSet(nid, true, 'edit');
            wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', 'New Draft version created. Change it, Save, then Recommend it for approval.', 'ok');
        } catch (err) { actionFailed(err); }
    }

    async function recommend(id) {
        const rows = await loadImpact(id);
        // gracUi.prompt(message, opts) -- grac-dialog.js (an options object
        // as the first argument showed "[object Object]").
        const note = await window.gracUi.prompt(
            (rows.length
                ? 'Approving this version will change ' + rows.length + ' audit(s):\n' + impactLines(rows) + '\n\n'
                : '') + 'What changed in this version? (optional)',
            { title: 'Recommend for approval', multiline: true, confirmText: 'Recommend' });
        if (note === null) return;
        try {
            await setAction(id, 'submit', { note: note || null });
            await afterAction(id, 'view', 'Recommended for approval.');
        } catch (err) { actionFailed(err); }
    }

    async function approve(id) {
        const rows = await loadImpact(id);
        if (!await window.gracUi.confirm(
              'Approve this question set version? It becomes the Active version.'
              + (rows.length ? '\n\nThese audits use an older version and will change:\n' + impactLines(rows)
                             + '\n\nA new audit version needs Submit for Review and Approve again.' : ''),
              { type: rows.length ? 'warning' : 'confirm', title: 'Approve question set', confirmText: 'Approve' })) return;
        try {
            const j = await setAction(id, 'approve');
            const defs = j.definitions || j.Definitions || [];
            const made = defs.filter(function (d) { return pick(d, 'actionCode', 'ActionCode') === 'NEW_VERSION'; });
            const moved = defs.length - made.length;
            let text = 'Approved. This version is now Active.';
            if (made.length) text += ' New audit version for review: ' + made.map(function (d) {
                return (pick(d, 'definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode') || '') + ' v' + (pick(d, 'newVersionNumber', 'NewVersionNumber') || '');
            }).join(', ') + '.';
            if (moved) text += ' ' + moved + ' audit draft(s) moved to this version.';
            await afterAction(id, 'view', text);
        } catch (err) { actionFailed(err); }
    }

    async function returnToDraft(id) {
        const reason = await window.gracUi.prompt('Reason (optional):', { title: 'Return to Draft', multiline: true, confirmText: 'Return' });
        if (reason === null) return;
        try {
            await setAction(id, 'return', { note: reason || null });
            await afterAction(id, 'view', 'Returned to Draft.');
        } catch (err) { actionFailed(err); }
    }

    async function discardDraft(id) {
        if (!await window.gracUi.confirm('Discard this Draft version and its questions? The Active version is not changed.',
              { type: 'warning', title: 'Discard draft', confirmText: 'Discard' })) return;
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/question-sets/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId)),
                { method: 'DELETE', credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
            if (!document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden) showList();
            else reloadSets();
            wf.setMessage('qsListMessage', 'Draft discarded.', 'ok');
        } catch (err) { actionFailed(err); }
    }
    function closeRowMenu() {
        if (openMenuEl)      { openMenuEl.remove(); openMenuEl = null; }
        if (openMenuTrigger) { openMenuTrigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'); openMenuTrigger = null; }
    }
    function openRowMenu(trg, items) {
        closeRowMenu();
        openMenuTrigger = trg;
        trg.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        openMenuEl = document.createElement('div');
        openMenuEl.className = 'pm-action-menu';
        openMenuEl.setAttribute('role', 'menu');
        items.forEach(function (it) {
            const b = document.createElement('button');
            b.type = 'button'; b.setAttribute('role', 'menuitem');
            b.innerHTML = '<i class="fa-solid ' + wf.escape(it.icon) + '" aria-hidden="true"></i> ' + wf.escape(it.label);
            b.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
                closeRowMenu();
                try { it.action(); } catch (err) { console.error('[question-sets] menu action failed', err); }
            });
            openMenuEl.appendChild(b);
        });
        document.body.appendChild(openMenuEl);
        const r = trg.getBoundingClientRect(), mr = openMenuEl.getBoundingClientRect(), gap = 6;
        let top = r.bottom + gap, left = r.right - mr.width;
        if (top + mr.height > window.innerHeight - 8) top = Math.max(8, r.top - mr.height - gap);
        if (left < 8) left = 8;
        if (left + mr.width > window.innerWidth - 8) left = window.innerWidth - mr.width - 8;
        openMenuEl.style.top = top + 'px'; openMenuEl.style.left = left + 'px';
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Set page
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function showList() {
        state.setId = null; state.rows = []; state.dirty = false;
        document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden = true;
        document.getElementById('qsListView').hidden = false;
        wf.setMessage('qsListMessage', '');
        reloadSets();
    }
    async function leaveSetPage() {
        if (document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden || state.mode !== 'edit' || !state.dirty) return true;
        return await window.gracUi.confirm('Leave this set without saving your changes?',
            { type: 'warning', title: 'Unsaved changes', confirmText: 'Leave' });
    }

    async function openSet(id, force, mode) {
        if (!force && !(await leaveSetPage())) return;
        state.mode = mode === 'edit' ? 'edit' : 'view';
        wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', '');
        state.setId = id ? String(id) : null;
        state.rows = [];
        const code = document.getElementById('qsSetCode');
        if (state.setId) {
            try {
                const org = encodeURIComponent(state.orgId), sid = encodeURIComponent(state.setId);
                const res = await Promise.all([
                    fetch(U(API + '/question-sets/' + sid + '?organizationId=' + org), { credentials: 'same-origin' }),
                    fetch(U(API + '/question-sets/' + sid + '/questions?organizationId=' + org), { credentials: 'same-origin' })
                ]);
                if (!res[0].ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + res[0].status);
                const d = ((await res[0].json()) || {});
                const set = d.data || d.Data || {};
                // The questions must load: an empty grid saved over a set
                // whose questions failed to load would remove them all.
                const qb = await safeJson(res[1]);
                if (!res[1].ok) throw new Error('its questions could not be loaded -- '
                    + ((qb && (qb.error || qb.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + res[1].status)));
                const qs = (qb && (qb.data || qb.Data)) || [];
                state.set = set;
                code.value = pick(set, 'setCode', 'SetCode') || '';
                code.disabled = true;                                   // fixed after create
                document.getElementById('qsSetName').value = pick(set, 'setName', 'SetName') || '';
                document.getElementById('qsSetStatus').value = pick(set, 'status', 'Status') || 'Active';
                document.getElementById('qsSetDescription').value = pick(set, 'description', 'Description') || '';
                state.rows = qs.map(function (q) { return fromServer(q); });
            } catch (err) {
                const msg = 'Could not open the question set: ' + (err.message || err);
                wf.setMessage('qsListMessage', msg, 'error');
                wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', msg, 'error');   // when already on the set page (after a Save)
                return;
            }
        } else {
            state.set = null;
            code.value = ''; code.disabled = false;
            document.getElementById('qsSetName').value = '';
            document.getElementById('qsSetStatus').value = 'Active';
            document.getElementById('qsSetDescription').value = '';
            state.rows = [newRow()];
        }
        state.dirty = !state.setId;
        const editing = state.mode === 'edit';
        document.getElementById('qsSetRead').hidden = editing;
        document.getElementById('qsSetEdit').hidden = !editing;
        // 551: the version status replaces the old Status choice.
        document.getElementById('qsSetStatusField').hidden = true;
        document.getElementById('qsActionsBtn').hidden = editing || !state.setId;
        document.getElementById('qsListView').hidden = true;
        document.getElementById('qsSetView').hidden = false;
        if (editing) renderGrid(); else renderRead();
        syncDirty();
        // 551: only a Draft version is edited.
        if (editing && state.setId && versionInfo(state.setId).status !== 'Draft') {
            openSet(state.setId, true, 'view');
            wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', 'Only a Draft version can be changed. Use New Version to change an approved question set.', 'error');
        }
    }

    // View mode: the set and its questions, read-only.
    function renderRead() {
        const s = state.set || {};
        const fmt = function (v) {
            if (!v) return '';
            if (typeof window.gracFormatDisplayDate === 'function') { const g = window.gracFormatDisplayDate(v); if (g !== v) return g; }
            return String(v).slice(0, 10);
        };
        const vno = pick(s, 'versionNumber', 'VersionNumber');
        const by = function (who, when) { return [who, fmt(when)].filter(Boolean).join(', '); };
        const facts = [
            ['Code', pick(s, 'setCode', 'SetCode')],
            ['Name', pick(s, 'setName', 'SetName')],
            ['Version', vno ? 'v' + vno : ''],                                            // 551
            ['Status', statusLabel(pick(s, 'versionStatus', 'VersionStatus') || pick(s, 'status', 'Status') || 'Active')],
            ['Questions', String(state.rows.length)],
            ['Recommended', by(pick(s, 'submittedBy', 'SubmittedBy'), pick(s, 'submittedDt', 'SubmittedDt'))],
            ['Approved', by(pick(s, 'approvedBy', 'ApprovedBy'), pick(s, 'approvedDt', 'ApprovedDt'))],
            ['Change Note', pick(s, 'changeNote', 'ChangeNote'), true],
            ['Description', pick(s, 'description', 'Description'), true],
            ['Created By', pick(s, 'enteredBy', 'EnteredBy')],
            ['Created', fmt(pick(s, 'enteredDt', 'EnteredDt'))],
            ['Updated By', pick(s, 'updatedBy', 'UpdatedBy')],
            ['Updated', fmt(pick(s, 'updatedDt', 'UpdatedDt'))]
        ];
        document.getElementById('qsReadFacts').innerHTML = facts.map(function (f) {
            return '<div' + (f[2] ? ' class="qs-wide"' : '') + '><dt>' + wf.escape(f[0]) + '</dt>'
                 + (f[1] ? '<dd>' + wf.escape(f[1]) + '</dd>' : '<dd class="qs-empty">Not set</dd>') + '</div>';
        }).join('');
        document.getElementById('qsReadCount').textContent = String(state.rows.length);
        const tick = '<i class="fa-solid fa-check" style="color:var(--success-700);" aria-label="Yes"></i>';
        document.getElementById('qsReadBody').innerHTML = state.rows.length ? state.rows.map(function (r, i) {
            const t = typeById(r.typeId);
            const sub = [r.help ? 'Testing guidance: ' + r.help : '', r.expected ? 'Expected evidence: ' + r.expected : '']
                .filter(Boolean).join('\n');
            return '<tr><td>' + wf.escape(r.code) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(r.text) + (sub ? '<div class="qs-read-sub">' + wf.escape(sub) + '</div>' : '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(t ? (pick(t, 'name', 'Name') || '') : (r.typeName || '')) + '</td>'
                 + '<td style="text-align:center;">' + (r.mandatory ? tick : '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(evidenceName(r)) + '</td>'
                 + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + wf.escape(r.weight) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(r.status || 'Active') + '</td></tr>';
        }).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">No questions in this version yet.'
                       + (versionInfo(state.setId).status === 'Draft' ? ' Use Actions &rsaquo; Edit to add some.' : '') + '</td></tr>';
        renderImpact();
        renderVersions();
    }

    // 551: for a Draft / Under Review version -- the audits using another
    // version of the set and what approving this one does to each.
    async function renderImpact() {
        const box = document.getElementById('qsImpact');
        const vs = versionInfo(state.setId).status;
        box.hidden = true;
        if (vs !== 'Draft' && vs !== 'UnderReview') return;
        const sid = state.setId;
        const rows = await loadImpact(sid);
        if (String(sid) !== String(state.setId) || !rows.length) return;
        document.getElementById('qsImpactCount').textContent = String(rows.length);
        document.getElementById('qsImpactNote').textContent =
            rows.length + ' audit(s) use an older version of this question set. Approving this version moves them to it'
            + ' -- an audit that is Active gets a new version that needs Submit for Review and Approve again.';
        document.getElementById('qsImpactBody').innerHTML = rows.map(function (d) {
            return '<tr><td>' + wf.escape((pick(d, 'definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode') || '') + ' ' + (pick(d, 'definitionName', 'DefinitionName') || '')) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>v' + wf.escape(pick(d, 'currentVersionNumber', 'CurrentVersionNumber') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.badge(pick(d, 'currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>v' + wf.escape(pick(d, 'linkedSetVersion', 'LinkedSetVersion') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(pick(d, 'actionText', 'ActionText') || '') + '</td></tr>';
        }).join('');
        box.hidden = false;
    }

    // 551: the set's versions, newest first; a row opens that version.
    async function renderVersions() {
        const body = document.getElementById('qsVersionBody');
        const sid = state.setId;
        body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="6" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        let rows = [];
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/question-sets/' + encodeURIComponent(sid) + '/versions?organizationId='
                + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId)), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const b = r.ok ? await r.json() : null;
            rows = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
        } catch (_) { rows = []; }
        if (String(sid) !== String(state.setId)) return;
        const fmt = function (who, when) {
            if (!when) return '';
            const d = typeof window.gracFormatDisplayDate === 'function' ? window.gracFormatDisplayDate(when) : String(when).slice(0, 10);
            return wf.escape([who, d].filter(Boolean).join(', '));
        };
        body.innerHTML = rows.length ? rows.map(function (v) {
            const id = pick(v, 'questionSetId', 'QuestionSetId');
            const cur = String(id) === String(state.setId);
            return '<tr class="pm-row-clickable' + (cur ? ' qs-version-current is-selected' : '') + '" data-version-id="' + wf.escape(id) + '">'
                 + '<td>v' + wf.escape(pick(v, 'versionNumber', 'VersionNumber')) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.badge(statusLabel(pick(v, 'versionStatus', 'VersionStatus'))) + '</td>'
                 + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + wf.escape(String(pick(v, 'questionCount', 'QuestionCount') || 0)) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(pick(v, 'changeNote', 'ChangeNote') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + fmt(pick(v, 'submittedBy', 'SubmittedBy'), pick(v, 'submittedDt', 'SubmittedDt')) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + fmt(pick(v, 'approvedBy', 'ApprovedBy'), pick(v, 'approvedDt', 'ApprovedDt')) + '</td></tr>';
        }).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="6" class="pm-empty">No versions.</td></tr>';
    }

    function fromServer(q) {
        const wt = pick(q, 'weight', 'Weight');
        return {
            key       : ++rowKey,
            questionId: pick(q, 'questionId', 'QuestionId'),
            code      : pick(q, 'questionCode', 'QuestionCode') || '',
            text      : pick(q, 'questionText', 'QuestionText') || '',
            help      : pick(q, 'helpText', 'HelpText') || '',
            typeId    : pick(q, 'questionTypeId', 'QuestionTypeId'),
            typeName  : pick(q, 'questionTypeName', 'QuestionTypeName') || '',
            mandatory : !!pick(q, 'isMandatory', 'IsMandatory'),
            evidenceTypeId  : pick(q, 'evidenceTypeId', 'EvidenceTypeId') || '',
            evidenceTypeName: pick(q, 'evidenceTypeName', 'EvidenceTypeName') || '',
            expected  : pick(q, 'expectedEvidence', 'ExpectedEvidence') || '',
            weight    : wt == null ? '' : String(wt),
            status    : pick(q, 'status', 'Status') || 'Active',
            version   : pick(q, 'versionNumber', 'VersionNumber') || 1,
            open      : false,
            state     : 'saved'
        };
    }
    function newRow() {
        return { key: ++rowKey, questionId: null, code: '', text: '', help: '', typeId: '', mandatory: false,
                 evidenceTypeId: '', evidenceTypeName: '', expected: '', weight: '', status: 'Active', version: null, open: false, state: 'new' };
    }

    function renderGrid() {
        const body = document.getElementById('qsGridBody');
        document.getElementById('qsQuestionCount').textContent = String(state.rows.length);
        if (!state.rows.length) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">No questions. Click "Add Row" to add one.</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        const yesNo = function (field, v) {
            return '<select class="pm-input" data-f="' + field + '"><option value="true"' + (v ? ' selected' : '') + '>Yes</option>'
                 + '<option value="false"' + (!v ? ' selected' : '') + '>No</option></select>';
        };
        body.innerHTML = state.rows.map(function (r, i) {
            const cls = r.state === 'new' ? 'qs-new' : (r.state === 'edit' ? 'qs-edit' : '');
            return '<tr data-key="' + r.key + '" class="' + cls + '">'
                 + '<td><input class="pm-input" type="text" maxlength="80" data-f="code" value="' + wf.escape(r.code) + '"'
                 +      (r.questionId ? ' disabled title="Code is fixed once saved"' : '') + ' aria-label="Code" /></td>'
                 + '<td><textarea class="pm-input" rows="1" maxlength="4000" data-f="text" aria-label="Question">' + wf.escape(r.text) + '</textarea></td>'
                 + '<td><select class="pm-input" data-f="typeId" aria-label="Response Type">' + typeOptions(r.typeId) + '</select></td>'
                 + '<td>' + yesNo('mandatory', r.mandatory) + '</td>'
                 + '<td><select class="pm-input" data-f="evidenceTypeId" aria-label="Evidence">' + evidenceOptions(r.evidenceTypeId) + '</select></td>'
                 + '<td><input class="pm-input" type="number" step="0.01" min="0" data-f="weight" value="' + wf.escape(r.weight) + '" aria-label="Weight" /></td>'
                 + '<td><select class="pm-input" data-f="status" aria-label="Status">'
                 +     ['Active', 'Inactive'].map(function (s) {
                           return '<option value="' + s + '"' + ((r.status || 'Active') === s ? ' selected' : '') + '>' + s + '</option>';
                       }).join('')
                 + '</select></td>'
                 + '<td class="qs-row-tools">'
                 +     '<button type="button" class="pm-button" data-act="more" title="Testing Guidance / Expected Evidence" aria-expanded="' + (r.open ? 'true' : 'false') + '">'
                 +     '<i class="fa-solid ' + (r.open ? 'fa-chevron-up' : 'fa-chevron-down') + '" aria-hidden="true"></i></button> '
                 +     '<button type="button" class="pm-button" data-act="remove" title="Remove row"><i class="fa-solid fa-trash" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>'
                 + '</td></tr>'
                 + '<tr class="qs-more" data-more="' + r.key + '"' + (r.open ? '' : ' hidden') + '><td colspan="8">'
                 +     '<div class="qs-more-fields">'
                 +     '<label class="pm-field"><span>Testing Guidance</span><textarea class="pm-input" rows="4" maxlength="20000" data-f="help">' + wf.escape(r.help) + '</textarea></label>'
                 +     '<label class="pm-field"><span>Expected Evidence</span><textarea class="pm-input" rows="4" maxlength="4000" data-f="expected">' + wf.escape(r.expected) + '</textarea></label>'
                 +     '</div></td></tr>';
        }).join('');
        body.querySelectorAll('textarea[data-f="text"]').forEach(autoSize);
    }

    // The Question cell grows with its text (no scrollbar, no drag handle).
    function autoSize(ta) {
        ta.style.height = 'auto';
        ta.style.height = Math.max(48, ta.scrollHeight) + 'px';
    }

    function rowOf(el) {
        const tr = el.closest('tr[data-key], tr[data-more]');
        if (!tr) return null;
        const key = Number(tr.getAttribute('data-key') || tr.getAttribute('data-more'));
        return state.rows.find(function (r) { return r.key === key; }) || null;
    }

    function onGridEdit(e) {
        const f = e.target.getAttribute && e.target.getAttribute('data-f');
        if (!f) return;
        const r = rowOf(e.target);
        if (!r) return;
        const v = e.target.value;
        if (f === 'text') autoSize(e.target);
        if (f === 'mandatory') r[f] = v === 'true';
        else r[f] = v;
        if (r.state === 'saved') {
            r.state = 'edit';
            const tr = document.querySelector('#qsGridBody tr[data-key="' + r.key + '"]');
            if (tr) tr.classList.add('qs-edit');
        }
        markDirty();
    }

    async function onGridClick(e) {
        const btn = e.target.closest('button[data-act]');
        if (!btn) return;
        const r = rowOf(btn);
        if (!r) return;
        if (btn.getAttribute('data-act') === 'more') {
            r.open = !r.open;
            renderGrid();
            return;
        }
        if (btn.getAttribute('data-act') === 'remove') {
            if (r.questionId && !await window.gracUi.confirm(
                  'Remove question ' + (r.code || '') + ' from this set? It is removed when you Save.',
                  { type: 'warning', title: 'Remove question', confirmText: 'Remove' })) return;
            state.rows.splice(state.rows.indexOf(r), 1);
            markDirty();
            renderGrid();
        }
    }

    function addRow() {
        const r = newRow();
        state.rows.push(r);
        markDirty();
        renderGrid();
        const input = document.querySelector('#qsGridBody tr[data-key="' + r.key + '"] input[data-f="code"]');
        if (input) input.focus();
    }

    function markDirty() { state.dirty = true; syncDirty(); }
    function syncDirty() { document.getElementById('qsDirtyNote').hidden = !state.dirty; }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Save: the details, then the whole grid.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    let saving = false;
    async function save() {
        if (saving) return;
        wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', '');
        const code = document.getElementById('qsSetCode').value.trim();
        const name = document.getElementById('qsSetName').value.trim();
        if (!code || !name) { wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', 'Code and Name of the question set are required.', 'error'); return; }

        // Grid checks before anything is written.
        const seen = {};
        for (let i = 0; i < state.rows.length; i++) {
            const r = state.rows[i], n = 'Row ' + (i + 1) + ': ';
            if (!String(r.code).trim()) { wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', n + 'Code is required.', 'error'); return; }
            if (!String(r.text).trim()) { wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', n + 'Question is required.', 'error'); return; }
            if (!r.typeId)              { wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', n + 'Response Type is required.', 'error'); return; }
            if (r.weight !== '' && !isFinite(Number(r.weight))) { wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', n + 'Weight must be a number.', 'error'); return; }
            const k = String(r.code).trim().toLowerCase();
            if (seen[k]) { wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', 'Code "' + r.code + '" is used on more than one row.', 'error'); return; }
            seen[k] = true;
        }

        saving = true;
        const btn = document.getElementById('qsSaveBtn'); btn.disabled = true;
        try {
            // 1. Set details (create or update). Owner is not asked any
            //    more; a set that has one keeps it.
            const j1 = await postJson('/question-sets', {
                organizationId   : Number(state.orgId),
                questionSetId    : state.setId ? Number(state.setId) : null,
                setCode          : code,
                setName          : name,
                description      : document.getElementById('qsSetDescription').value || null,
                ownerEmployeeId  : pick(state.set, 'ownerEmployeeId', 'OwnerEmployeeId') || null,
                ownerDisplayName : pick(state.set, 'ownerDisplayName', 'OwnerDisplayName') || null,
                status           : pick(state.set, 'status', 'Status') || 'Active',   // 551: version status rules instead
                actor            : null
            });
            const setId = String(j1.questionSetId || j1.QuestionSetId || state.setId);
            // The set exists from here on: a failure below must not create it again.
            state.setId = setId;
            document.getElementById('qsSetCode').disabled = true;

            // 2. The whole grid, in its on-screen order.
            await postJson('/question-sets/' + encodeURIComponent(setId) + '/questions/grid', {
                organizationId : Number(state.orgId),
                questions      : state.rows.map(function (r, i) {
                    const t = typeById(r.typeId);
                    return {
                        questionId       : r.questionId || null,
                        questionCode     : String(r.code).trim(),
                        questionText     : String(r.text).trim(),
                        helpText         : r.help || null,
                        questionTypeId   : Number(r.typeId),
                        questionTypeCode : t ? (pick(t, 'code', 'Code') || null) : null,
                        questionTypeName : t ? (pick(t, 'name', 'Name') || null) : null,
                        isMandatory      : !!r.mandatory,
                        evidenceTypeId   : r.evidenceTypeId ? Number(r.evidenceTypeId) : null,   // null = Not Applicable
                        expectedEvidence : r.expected || null,
                        weight           : r.weight === '' ? null : Number(r.weight),
                        status           : r.status || 'Active',   // 561: chosen on every row, a new row too
                        displayOrder     : i + 1
                    };
                }),
                actor          : null
            });

            state.dirty = false;
            await openSet(setId, true, 'view');         // saved: back to the view
            wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', 'Question set saved.', 'ok');
        } catch (err) {
            wf.setMessage('qsSetMessage', err.message || String(err), 'error');
        } finally {
            saving = false; btn.disabled = false;
        }
    }

    async function postJson(path, body) {
        const r = await fetch(U(API + path), {
            method: 'POST', credentials: 'same-origin',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify(body)
        });
        const j = await safeJson(r);
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
        return j || {};
    }
    async function safeJson(r) { try { return await r.json(); } catch (_) { return null; } }
})();
</script>
